    {"id":"docs_scriptedtrade_docs_models_heston_model","label":"Heston Model","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/ScriptedTrade/docs/models.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Multi-asset Heston correlations use a 'parsimonious' partial-independence approach for spot-variance/variance-variance correlations across assets since these are not directly observable, and QuantLib's two-independent-Wiener-process Heston implementation requires an explicit decorrelation step to recover the desired correlated increments."},
